From f3f365f30dad4881771b19d3dbc4e3786ba1e699 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tomaz Zaman <tomaz@mono.si>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 13:23:45 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] netfilter: flowtable: offer again a flow whose neighbour was
 resolving

flow_offload_work_add() builds both directions' rules before it asks any
driver, and gives up on the whole flow when either cannot be built. One
that often cannot is a neighbour still resolving: a connection is
offered by its first packet after confirmation, for a request and its
response the first reply, which can be the first packet sent to its
destination.

Software offers the flow again on its next refresh, about a second
later. A table with hardware handles keeps every packet off the software
fast path while any XFRM policy or blocking default is configured, so
nothing refreshes such a flow, and the connection stays in software
until the flow expires -- 30 seconds for UDP -- and is added afresh.

Invalidate the flow's handle when its rules fail on a neighbour still
resolving and nothing will refresh it. GC retires the generation, and
the connection's next packet offers a fresh one. A failed neighbour, or
any other failure to build the rules, waits for the flow to expire: a
retry would only meet the same refusal.

Signed-off-by: Tomaz Zaman <tomaz@mono.si>
---
 net/netfilter/nf_flow_table_offload.c | 16 +++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 15 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/net/netfilter/nf_flow_table_offload.c b/net/netfilter/nf_flow_table_offload.c
index 0c09e70..bbdc658 100644
--- a/net/netfilter/nf_flow_table_offload.c
+++ b/net/netfilter/nf_flow_table_offload.c
@@ -363,8 +363,22 @@ static int flow_offload_eth_dst(struct net *net,
 		read_unlock_bh(&n->lock);
 		neigh_release(n);
 
-		if (!(nud_state & NUD_VALID))
+		if (!(nud_state & NUD_VALID)) {
+			/* A neighbour still resolving fails both directions'
+			 * rules, and software offers the flow again on its next
+			 * refresh. While a policy keeps every packet of a table
+			 * with hardware handles off the software fast path
+			 * (xfrm_flowtable_enabled()) nothing refreshes it: retire
+			 * the generation, so that GC removes it and the
+			 * connection's next packet offers a fresh one. A failed
+			 * neighbour waits for the flow to expire, as a refusal
+			 * that would only recur.
+			 */
+			if (!(nud_state & NUD_FAILED) &&
+			    !xfrm_flowtable_enabled(net))
+				nf_flow_offload_handle_invalidate(flow->hw_handle);
 			return -ENOENT;
+		}
 		break;
 	default:
 		return -EOPNOTSUPP;
